IMPORT prelude

-- coa28-part45.l4: Part 45 (Northern Ireland), ss 1284-1287 of the Companies Act 2006,
-- lines 18505-18530 of ukpga-2006-46.txt (a plain-text rendering from legislation.gov.uk; not the official text).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Part 45 extends the Companies Acts, and some Great Britain enactments on other forms of
-- business organisation, to Northern Ireland and ends the Northern Ireland instruments they replace. The text of each
-- section does not itself say when it takes effect: that is s 1300(2) (commencement by order, inert in NOTES.md), so
-- every answer says what the section provides and no more.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words (FALSE-kind comments), NOTHING
-- otherwise (NOTHING-kind comments). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

-- ---- s 1284: Extension of Companies Acts to Northern Ireland ---------------------------------------------------

-- src:18507 | (1) The Companies Acts as defined by this Act (see section 2) extend to Northern Ireland.
@ref s 1284(1) Extension of Companies Acts to Northern Ireland (src:18507)
GIVEN `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1284(1) the provision extends to Northern Ireland` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Companies Acts as defined by this Act (see section 2) extend to Northern Ireland" says nothing of other provisions
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the provision is one of the Companies Acts is the answer of s 2(1), supplied by the caller

DECLARE `s 1284(2) instrument` IS ONE OF
    `s 1284(2) the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6))`
    `s 1284(2) the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1035 (N.I. 9))`
    `s 1284(2) Part 3 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Order 2005 (S.I. 2005/1967 (N.I. 17))`
    `s 1284(2) another instrument`

-- src:18508 | (2) The Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6)), the Companies Consolidation (Consequential Provisions) (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1035 (N.I. 9)) and Part 3 of the Companies (Audit, Investigations and Community Enterprise) Order 2005 (S.I. 2005/1967 (N.I. 17)) shall cease to have effect accordingly.
@ref s 1284(2) Extension of Companies Acts to Northern Ireland (src:18508)
GIVEN instrument IS A `s 1284(2) instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1284(2) the instrument ceases to have effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `s 1284(2) another instrument` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall cease to have effect accordingly" names three instruments and no others
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 1285: Extension of GB enactments relating to UK Societas -------------------------------------------------

-- src:18510 | (1) The enactments in force in Great Britain relating to UK Societas extend to Northern Ireland.
@ref s 1285(1) Extension of GB enactments relating to UK Societas (src:18510)
GIVEN `the enactment is in force in Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment relates to UK Societas` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1285(1) the enactment extends to Northern Ireland` MEANS
    IF `the enactment is in force in Great Britain` AND `the enactment relates to UK Societas`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The enactments in force in Great Britain relating to UK Societas extend to Northern Ireland"

DECLARE `s 1285(2) enactment` IS ONE OF
    `s 1285(2)(a) the European Public Limited-Liability Company Regulations (Northern Ireland) 2004 (SR 2004/417)`
    `s 1285(2)(b) the European Public Limited-Liability Company (Fees) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 2004 (SR 2004/418)`
    `s 1285(2) another enactment`

-- src:18511 | (2) The following enactments shall cease to have effect accordingly—
-- src:18512 | (a) the European Public Limited-Liability Company Regulations (Northern Ireland) 2004 (SR 2004/417), and
-- src:18513 | (b) the European Public Limited-Liability Company (Fees) Regulations (Northern Ireland) 2004 (SR 2004/418).
@ref s 1285(2) Extension of GB enactments relating to UK Societas (src:18511-18513)
GIVEN enactment IS A `s 1285(2) enactment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1285(2) the enactment ceases to have effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER enactment
    WHEN `s 1285(2) another enactment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The following enactments shall cease to have effect accordingly" names two enactments and no others
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:18514 | (3) In this section “UK Societas” means a United Kingdom Societas within the meaning of Council Regulation 2157/2001/EC of 8 October 2001 on the Statute for a European Company.
@ref s 1285(3) Extension of GB enactments relating to UK Societas (src:18514)
GIVEN `the entity is a United Kingdom Societas within the meaning of Council Regulation 2157/2001/EC of 8 October 2001 on the Statute for a European Company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1285(3) the entity is a UK Societas` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entity is a United Kingdom Societas within the meaning of Council Regulation 2157/2001/EC of 8 October 2001 on the Statute for a European Company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“UK Societas” means a United Kingdom Societas within the meaning of Council Regulation 2157/2001/EC"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Council Regulation is not among the sources

-- ---- s 1286: Extension of GB enactments relating to certain other forms of business organisation -------------------

-- The text of 1286(1)(c) ends "open-ended investment companies, ..." in the rendering: the ellipsis marks words the
-- text no longer shows; no list item is repealed.
DECLARE `s 1286(1) form of business organisation` IS ONE OF
    `s 1286(1)(a) limited liability partnerships`
    `s 1286(1)(b) limited partnerships`
    `s 1286(1)(c) open-ended investment companies`
    `s 1286(1)(d) European Economic Interest Groupings`
    `s 1286(1)(e) UK Economic Interest Groupings`
    `s 1286(1) another form of business organisation`

-- src:18516 | (1) The enactments in force in Great Britain relating to—
-- src:18517 | (a) limited liability partnerships,
-- src:18518 | (b) limited partnerships,
-- src:18519 | (c) open-ended investment companies, ...
-- src:18520 | (d) European Economic Interest Groupings, and
-- src:18521 | (e) UK Economic Interest Groupings,
-- src:18522 | extend to Northern Ireland.
@ref s 1286(1) Extension of GB enactments relating to certain other forms of business organisation (src:18516-18522)
GIVEN form IS A `s 1286(1) form of business organisation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1286(1) the enactments in force in Great Britain relating to the form extend to Northern Ireland` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `s 1286(1) another form of business organisation` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The enactments in force in Great Britain relating to— (a) ... (e) extend to Northern Ireland" names five forms and no others
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 1286(2) enactment` IS ONE OF
    `s 1286(2)(a) the Limited Liability Partnerships Act (Northern Ireland) 2002 (c. 12 (N. I.))`
    `s 1286(2)(b) the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 (c. 24) as it formerly had effect in Northern Ireland`
    `s 1286(2)(c) the Open-Ended Investment Companies Act (Northern Ireland) 2002 (c. 13 (N.I.))`
    `s 1286(2)(d) the European Economic Interest Groupings Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1989 (SR 1989/216)`
    `s 1286(2) another enactment`

-- src:18523 | (2) The following enactments shall cease to have effect accordingly—
-- src:18524 | (a) the Limited Liability Partnerships Act (Northern Ireland) 2002 (c. 12 (N. I.));
-- src:18525 | (b) the Limited Partnerships Act 1907 (c. 24) as it formerly had effect in Northern Ireland;
-- src:18526 | (c) the Open-Ended Investment Companies Act (Northern Ireland) 2002 (c. 13 (N.I.));
-- src:18527 | (d) the European Economic Interest Groupings Regulations (Northern Ireland) 1989 (SR 1989/216).
@ref s 1286(2) Extension of GB enactments relating to certain other forms of business organisation (src:18523-18527)
GIVEN enactment IS A `s 1286(2) enactment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1286(2) the enactment ceases to have effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER enactment
    WHEN `s 1286(2) another enactment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The following enactments shall cease to have effect accordingly" names four enactments and no others
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 1287: Extension of enactments relating to business names ---------------------------------------------------

-- src:18529 | (1) The provisions of Part 41 of this Act (business names) extend to Northern Ireland.
@ref s 1287(1) Extension of enactments relating to business names (src:18529)
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of Part 41 of this Act (business names)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1287(1) the provision extends to Northern Ireland` MEANS
    IF `the provision is a provision of Part 41 of this Act (business names)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of Part 41 of this Act (business names) extend to Northern Ireland"

DECLARE `s 1287(2) instrument` IS ONE OF
    `s 1287(2) the Business Names (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1033 (N.I. 7))`
    `s 1287(2) another instrument`

-- src:18530 | (2) The Business Names (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1033 (N.I. 7)) shall cease to have effect accordingly.
@ref s 1287(2) Extension of enactments relating to business names (src:18530)
GIVEN instrument IS A `s 1287(2) instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1287(2) the instrument ceases to have effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER instrument
    WHEN `s 1287(2) another instrument` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall cease to have effect accordingly" names one instrument and no other
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
